00:40:39.722 --> 00:40:44.687
This student is awarded the George C
Parker prize, named in honor of GSB

00:40:44.687 --> 00:40:49.752
faculty and former program director,
George Parker who is here today.

00:40:49.752 --> 00:40:50.373
George.

00:40:50.373 --> 00:40:53.314
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; There he is.

00:40:53.314 --> 00:40:58.645
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; The graduate receives a certificate,

00:40:58.645 --> 00:41:03.390
a cash award, and their name will be
on a plaque displayed at the GSB.

00:41:03.390 --> 00:41:09.063
The recipient of the George C Parker
prize is Abhishek Garg.

00:41:09.063 --> 00:41:14.549
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Please, please, please stand.

00:41:14.549 --> 00:41:20.823
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Please,

00:41:20.823 --> 00:41:24.005
there's Abhishek,
please stand and be recognized.

00:41:24.005 --> 00:41:26.480
Great, thank you very much.

00:41:26.480 --> 00:41:27.779
Congratulations.

00:41:27.779 --> 00:41:31.970
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; I am

00:41:31.970 --> 00:41:34.799
now going to move on to the MBA class.

00:41:34.799 --> 00:41:41.544
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:41:41.544 --> 00:41:44.648
&gt;&gt; Distinguished guests, faculty staff,

00:41:44.648 --> 00:41:50.333
family and friends, MBA class of 2020,
welcome back, we missed you.

00:41:50.333 --> 00:41:53.846
You finished under extraordinary and
difficult conditions and

00:41:53.846 --> 00:41:58.472
it's great to have this opportunity to
properly celebrate your accomplishments.

00:41:58.472 --> 00:42:03.796
The MBA students gathered before us today
engaged in a transformational experience.

00:42:03.796 --> 00:42:07.338
They acquired solid foundations
in general management and

00:42:07.338 --> 00:42:10.183
pursued deeper study in
the areas of interest.

00:42:10.183 --> 00:42:15.243
They engaged in personal growth and built
relationships that will last a lifetime.

00:42:15.243 --> 00:42:18.389
They have helped the school and
the community in many ways.

00:42:18.389 --> 00:42:22.590
While their experience here required
navigating the challenges of a global

00:42:22.590 --> 00:42:26.603
pandemic that changed classes and
other activities in countless ways.

00:42:26.603 --> 00:42:31.259
They persevered and formed bonds
that I expect will be stronger than

00:42:31.259 --> 00:42:33.963
the MBA classes that came before them.

00:42:33.963 --> 00:42:37.172
They're an impressive group and
are ready and

00:42:37.172 --> 00:42:40.802
worthy to join the ranks
of our illustrious alumni.

00:42:40.802 --> 00:42:46.018
Therefore, it is my great honor and
privilege to

00:42:46.018 --> 00:42:51.626
present to you the Standford MBA
class of 2020.

00:42:51.626 --> 00:42:57.983
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; I

00:42:57.983 --> 00:43:01.727
hope your memories of the GSB have and
will continue to remain fresh and

00:43:01.727 --> 00:43:04.148
that you will stay
involved with the school.

00:43:04.148 --> 00:43:07.927
Our alumni played an important
role in your academic experience,

00:43:07.927 --> 00:43:11.367
ranging from serving as judges
in the executive challenge,

00:43:11.367 --> 00:43:14.281
to acting as mentors in
entrepreneurial courses.

00:43:14.281 --> 00:43:19.219
I hope that you too will engage with
GSB's academic mission as alumni,

00:43:19.219 --> 00:43:23.765
and give your time and
experience generously to future classes.

00:43:23.765 --> 00:43:28.294
You will leave your own legacy and
play a part in bringing the GSB

00:43:28.294 --> 00:43:33.526
experience to future generations as
other alumni have done before you.

00:43:33.526 --> 00:43:38.061
On a somber note, I would like to
take a moment to remember your

00:43:38.061 --> 00:43:41.476
classmate Erica Pincus,
who died last June.

00:43:41.476 --> 00:43:48.344
In 2020, Erica earned her MBA from the GSB
and an MPA from Harvard's Kennedy School.

00:43:48.344 --> 00:43:51.214
It is heartbreaking that she
is not here with us today.

00:43:51.214 --> 00:43:57.716
We are grateful to be
joined by her parents and

00:43:57.716 --> 00:44:03.887
her close GSB friends to honor her memory.

00:44:03.887 --> 00:44:13.887
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:44:53.772 --> 00:44:58.051
&gt;&gt; There is a picture of Emma in the
program and a seat among the graduates,

00:44:58.051 --> 00:45:01.990
which is marked with a red ribbon
that would have been hers today.

00:45:01.990 --> 00:45:04.673
Thank you for honoring her that way.

00:45:04.673 --> 00:45:07.915
All of you here have undoubtedly
heard of Arjay Miller.

00:45:07.915 --> 00:45:11.556
Arjay served in the US Air Force
during the Second World War, and

00:45:11.556 --> 00:45:16.222
was later one of the so called Whiz Kids,
who revolutionized Ford Motor Company.

00:45:16.222 --> 00:45:20.993
Arjay became president of Ford,
and then later the much

00:45:20.993 --> 00:45:25.980
admired fourth dean of
the GSB from 1968 to 1978.

00:45:25.980 --> 00:45:30.455
In honor of Dean Miller's service,
the top 10% of the class rank

00:45:30.455 --> 00:45:34.944
by academic performance are designated
as RJ Miller's scholars.

00:45:34.944 --> 00:45:39.913
As we read the names of the graduates, we
will also announce if they have received

00:45:39.913 --> 00:45:43.145
the academic distinction
of Arjay Miller scholar.

00:45:43.145 --> 00:45:47.527
In the case of joint degree students who
are working today, but not graduating,

00:45:47.527 --> 00:45:51.404
we will identify those who are currently
in the top 10% of the class.

00:45:51.404 --> 00:45:55.795
The late Dean Miller also founded
the certificate in public management and

00:45:55.795 --> 00:45:58.104
social innovation program at the GSB.

00:45:58.104 --> 00:46:03.044
The certificate program educates
leaders who understand societal issues,

00:46:03.044 --> 00:46:07.528
design for and evaluate impact, and
understand the specificities of

00:46:07.528 --> 00:46:12.929
the management of social organizations in
both the private and the public sectors.

00:46:12.929 --> 00:46:17.118
Today's certificate graduates
take the spirit of our GSB motto,

00:46:17.118 --> 00:46:22.218
change lives, change organizations,
change the world to its full potential.

